 r"I am writing to apply for the Business MI \& Insight Analyst position at Clear Group. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have built dashboards and KPI frameworks that operational teams use, analysed what is driving performance, and turned the results into recommendations that leaders act on.",

 r"What attracts me most to this role is that the analysis has a visible end point: operational and commercial decisions across UK Retail that lead to better outcomes for clients and colleagues. The posting describes partnering with operations, sales and customer experience leaders to understand performance and find opportunities, which is the part of analytics I enjoy most. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse large merchant and transaction datasets in SQL and Python to find the drivers behind performance across the UK marketplace, and I build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Much of the work is helping stakeholders agree what a KPI should measure before building anything, and the recurring lesson has been that the first metric someone asks for is rarely the one that answers their question. I also used Claude Code to automate a repetitive campaign configuration task, which cut the time it took by around 40 to 50 percent.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern for a pharmaceutical client in a highly regulated healthcare setting. I worked with clinical experts to turn their safety requirements into a 246-question benchmark and scoring rubric, which the client adopted as its acceptance standard, built a pipeline that turned more than 4,800 free-text patient consultation threads into structured data, and presented the findings to clinical and business stakeholders. This taught me to define clear standards and measure performance against them, which is close to the kind of customer outcome monitoring Clear does under Consumer Duty.",

 r"My MSc dissertation used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants, which meant a great deal of time on data validation and on checking that results held up before presenting them. At Ipsos Strategy3 I analysed more than 80 healthcare professional interviews and turned the analysis into reports and recommendations for client teams. Both taught me to check the data before trusting any conclusion built on it.",

 r"I would bring Clear Group strong SQL and Power BI skills, experience building KPI frameworks and dashboards for operational teams, careful attention to data quality, and the ability to explain findings clearly to senior stakeholders. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship, and I am based in London.",

